iconv: add the z/OS XMLSS EBCDIC codepage set

Adds the complete EBCDIC SBCS set accepted by z/OS XML System Services
(and therefore by IBM Enterprise COBOL XML PARSE) beyond the in-tree
ibm1047: IBM037, 273, 277, 278, 280, 284, 285, 297, 500, 871, and the
euro variants 1140-1149.  Pure data in codepages.h, same elided-quad
packing as the in-tree ibm1047 entry; both conversion directions work
via the existing generic map paths.  Adds 6965 bytes to charmaps[].

Why: libxml2's encoding sniffer (xmlDetectEBCDIC) unconditionally opens
an IBM037 iconv handler for any EBCDIC-detected document, then the
document's declared codepage; gcc 16 libgcobol's codepage layer
(charmaps.cc) resolves EBCDIC CODEPAGE names through iconv_open.
Without these pages all EBCDIC XML fails and -fexec-charset=CP1140
(the gcobol man page's own example) is unusable.

Correctness: tables generated and cross-verified by tools/ebcdic/
(gen_codepages.py + verify.py).  Authority is glibc iconv cross-checked
byte-for-byte against ICU (IBM CDRA lineage) and Python codecs, with
five documented corrections where glibc's legacy tables are provably
wrong: IBM278 0x71/0xE0 (E-acute/backslash swapped), IBM285 0xA1
(overline vs macron), IBM871 0x4A/0xC0 (thorn case swapped).  Proof:
IBM defines each euro page as its base page with U+00A4 replaced by the
euro at one position, and glibc's own 1143/1146/1149 contradict its
278/285/871 at exactly those bytes while agreeing with ICU.  That
euro-sibling invariant holds for all ten pairs of this set.  One
tolerated third-party deviation: Python cp273 maps 0xBC to U+203E
where glibc/ICU say U+00AF.

Aliases follow musl fuzzycmp conventions; the euro pages carry both
ibm114x and ibm0114x spellings because the IANA names are IBM01140-
style and fuzzycmp does not ignore zeros.  Runtime coverage is gated by
the ebcdic-iconv probe in run-caps (per-page FNV-1a goldens emitted by
the same generator).

